  "limitations": "The first11 terminal trials used unrestricted scheduling and four Torch threads; the remaining29 used two concurrent workers, each pinned to four distinct physical cores with one SMT thread per core. The groups do not overlap physical cores. Memory bandwidth, CPU package power, frequency and host activity remain shared. These strata contain different cases and were not randomized between execution modes. Their timing, call counts, distances and success rates are descriptive; no same-case counterfactual establishes speedup, slowdown or an algorithmic gain. This is one seed and one confirmation photograph per each of ten classes. Imagenette may overlap VGG pretraining. All40 cases, including failures, remain in the total success denominator; every norm has ten cases. Distance units differ across norms and must not be compared across attacks. The confirmation bank is now consumed and must not be relabeled fresh after tuning.",
  "grading": "Mandatory attack+distance/render+classification uses180/300 seconds. Frozen optimizer165/270 targets are separate diagnostics. Failed cases retain999999999.",
  "timing_statistics": "Runtime totals are sums of recorded per-case wall times, not elapsed makespan or CPU seconds. Parallel case intervals overlap. Query totals are actual model-evaluation examples as recorded by each attack.",
